    "title": "Celtics vs Suns at TD Garden: How to watch Boston’s playoff push",
    "text": "March 16, 2026, 11:19 a.m. ETThe Boston Celtics only have 15 games left in their regular season schedule.The Celtics will play the Phoenix Suns tonight, March 16, 2026.The Celtics will play the Golden State Warriors later this week.The Boston Celtics walloped the Washington Wizards on Saturday night, and now, there are just 15 games left in the NBA regular season.Tonight, that final stretch starts with the Celtics playing the Phoenix Suns, who are 39-28 on the season, competing for a top-six spot in the NBA's Western Conference.The Celtics have a record of 44-23 and are second place in the Eastern Conference.Only a limited number of sports pundits picked the Celtics to do well this season, as Jayson Tatum was sidelined for most of the year with an Achilles injury until he returned two weeks ago.Will they make a strong run for the NBA Championship?The next step starts tonight against the Suns.Here's how to watch.What time is tipoff for the Celtics game tonight?The game will tip off at 7:30 p.m. ET.Where is the game being played?It'll be played at the TD Garden in Boston, home arena for the Celtics.How to watch tonight's Celtics gameYou can watch the game locally on NBC Sports Boston, or nationally on NBC. Fans can also stream the game on Peacock or on FuboTV.Watch the Celtics!People can also listen to the game on 98.5 the Sports Hub, or stream it via the station's app.Who do the Celtics play after they play the Suns?The Celtics will play the Golden State Warriors on Wednesday, March 18, 2026 at 7 p.m. at TD Garden in Boston.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
